# Tap feedback first - required check before any code (owner rule, Garen, Nov 16, 2026)

Before writing or changing any code, check every button, link, card, photo link and form you touch (and the others on the same screen):
1. Does it react in the same instant it is tapped or clicked?
2. Does it show a loading state if the next page, app or call is slow?
3. Does that feedback start BEFORE any other work (navigation, fetch, API call, tracking, analytics, state updates)?
If any answer is no, fix it as part of the change and say so in your report. This check is required, not optional.

## Rules
- The FIRST line of every tap/click/submit handler sets the pressed/loading state. Nothing runs before it. Never await anything before showing feedback.
- Let the browser paint first, then do the work: requestAnimationFrame(() => setTimeout(work, 0)).
- Tracking (gtag, Clarity, Meta, etc.) never blocks feedback or navigation; use beacon transport.
- Instant press state on every tappable: :active scale(0.97) + slightly darker, transition <= 100 ms. Never rely on :hover alone.
- touch-action: manipulation and -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent on tappables (no tap delay on phones).
- Loading state: small spinner (currentColor) + short text ("Opening...", "Loading...", "Sending..."). Same size as the button, no layout shift.
- aria-busy="true" while loading; block extra taps (no double navigation, no double submit).
- Internal links: prefetch, and keep the loading state until the route changes.
- External links (WhatsApp, booking, maps, phone, payment): show loading, then open; reset after 4 s if the page is still visible.
- Forms/API calls: disable the submit button and show a spinner at once; then show success or error.
- Reset loading states on "pageshow" (back/forward cache) so nothing stays stuck.
- prefers-reduced-motion: no scale or spin; use a color change + static text.
- Contrast >= 4.5:1 in every state.
- Mobile apps (React Native/Expo etc.): same rule - Pressable pressed style + ActivityIndicator first, then the action.

## Before finishing, test and report
- On a slow network (DevTools "Slow 4G"), tap every changed control: feedback shows within 100 ms.
- Double tap does not trigger twice. Going back shows normal buttons again.
- INP < 200 ms for these taps. No new console errors.